Many people claim that teenagers should spend less time playing games. While some teenagers may disagree, I firmly believe that it is not reasonable to play games too much. This essay will demonstrate this opinion through useful skills and health problems.

First and foremost, there are tons of useful skills which games cannot provide. Specifically, cooking, playing soccer or even farming if teenagers want to. If teenagers have less time in a flat screen, they could improve in real-life skills instead of gaming, which is not very essential for a normal teenager. 

The second main fact is about health problems, which is one of the most significant problems in all society. As an example, gaming every day without certain exercises will cause fatness and even lose the ability to walk if serious.

Admittedly, people might contend that games is very important in a teenager's life. But they overlook that teenagers are playing video games too much that it will efect certain health and acedamic problems.

In conclusion, despite concerns about not involved in society nowadays, I maintain that teenagers should reduce their screen time, for either skills or health.